===== SEED 3303 =====
Doubly-weighted zero-sum subsequence

All arithmetic in this problem is modulo M = 170265322778820731061211387556230497856.  The sequence below has
127 entries x_1,...,x_127.  Indices are 1-based.

The two allowed weight sets are singletons: A = {1} and B = {2660395668419073922831427930566101529}.  Thus a
chosen subsequence with indices I has fixed weights a_i=1 and b_i=2660395668419073922831427930566101529 and is
doubly-weighted zero-sum exactly when both congruences hold:

    sum(x_i for i in I) = 0 (mod M)
    sum(b_i*a_i for i in I) = 0 (mod M).

